{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: R5C (bearer items 4 and 5: fixed 30-day expiry, one-time disclosure, redacted receipts, bounded legacy migration, stream closure) at exact head 6015dc3d610da3f4769ecd8a2c00cc3bc59ee98c, tree 04c6013059c8d2d1251102f62edfaab6f70e4ce6 (review request fbac26ea, promise 9f814f41, implementation a3e54dcf / fb529297, policy 855dd86d). There is one required documentation finding, F1, of the same class as F1 in my slice A review 982a82b1 and slice B review f52cefdc. I found no code defect. A note-only successor carries the gate without a repeat (docs/testing.md:597); I will review it on arrival.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-hosted-mcp-bearer-expiry.md (artifact dcbb4505), first and in full. Then the whole diff against Main dbaa3a2a: hosted.ts, http.ts, hosted.scope.test.ts, http-idle.test.ts, docs/mcp.md, notes/2026-10-13-hosted-mcp-endpoint.md and the seal file. For the admission order I read HostedAgent.fetch, #authorized, #httpOf, #control_ and the create transaction, and ControlPlane.charge, complete, retained and expire at the head. The branch merges the landed R5B (27defd77), the diagnostic head (85029a09) and Main dbaa3a2a (e10584fc, the gate head, tree a0b8b3c0) and adds only the note at 6015dc3d (61 insertions, 7 deletions). The merge-base with Main is dbaa3a2a, the diff touches eight paths, and the act log holds a pointer at this head for each of them. Merging the head into Main dbaa3a2a gives exactly its tree, 04c60130.\n\nF1 (required, documentation). notes/2026-10-13-hosted-mcp-endpoint.md:134-135, in the new \"R5C bearer contract amendment\" section: \"The implementation note keeps validation pending.\" The implementation note it links to says the ordinary gate 11319 passed at e10584fc and that exact-head review and deployment remain pending. The sentence contradicts that note at this head and is false on Main once it lands. Requested fix: say that the implementation note records the implementation, its validation and the deployment obligations (explicit renewal of live tokens, registry activation or recorded lazy cleanup). A docs-only change, no code, no gate repeat.\n\nWhat the head does, against the conditions of a3e54dcf and decision 855dd86d:\n- Fixed lifetime. BEARER_LIFETIME_MS is 30 days. A new agent column bearer_expires is written at the create commit and at each fresh renewal from the issuance clock, cleared by retire, and touched by nothing else: use, replay, reset, configuration writes and receipt expiry leave it alone (#setConfig and #expire are unchanged).\n- Admission fails closed. #authorized requires an enrolled row with a digest, a parseable expiry and now strictly before it. A null (legacy) or malformed expiry refuses 401 before any MCP body; Origin 403 and the per-address failure window keep their precedence in fetch. The witness shows 200 one millisecond before expiry and 401 at it, after a reset.\n- One disclosure. The plaintext exists only in the committing transaction's return value. ControlPlane.complete redacts every stored answer (bearer removed, bearerShown true, bearerExpires kept), so the agent's control row and the registry's control row never hold it; the agent row stores the same redacted receipt. The registry settles its reservation once (state must still be reserved), and the agent's decided transaction hands a second concurrent caller the stored redacted answer. A reset after the commit replays the receipt and never remints: the witness shows the stored digest unchanged across the fence.\n- Replay. The same op returns its original status and the receipt; stale 409 after seven days and fingerprint 409 are unchanged. A later renewal does not rewrite the creation receipt (witness).\n- Migration. migrateBearerAnswers runs in both constructors under a marker row bearer-schema in the existing control_budget table: adds the column when absent, pages one stored answer at a time by op within the control budget, rewrites only answers that carry a bearer, credits the byte difference through the existing charge, leaves the uncharged agent-row duplicate uncredited, and commits as one transaction. The witness rebuilds the pre-cutover schema and accounting, aborts the last write with a SQL trigger and shows column, answers, credit and marker all rolled back; the retried migration redacts all three copies with the exact credit, and a second construction changes nothing. The registry's copy migrates only when that registry activates, which the note, docs/mcp.md and the endpoint note state as the planner's obligation.\n- Stream closure without alarms. McpHttp takes a lifetime port. #lifetime schedules min(30 s, remaining) only while a stream or listen is open and cancels when none is; a generation counter makes a stale callback harmless. closeAll is idempotent, marks the layer closed, cancels the timer, ends every session including ones still initializing before its first await, and completes listens. handle, #stream and #listen refuse 401 when due, before and after their awaits; #persist writes nothing once due or closed; abrupt marks closed and discarded. The agent discards its layer after create, renewal and retire, so the layer's expiry snapshot cannot outlive the row it was read from. Local servers pass no lifetime, so nothing changes for them.\n- Admitted calls finish. The witness holds the native send across the deadline: the admitted call settles once, the next call is refused, and custody has nothing unresolved.\n\nWitnesses in the gate (31 mcp C cases, all passed in terminal-cases.json): H1 under both register definitions asserts the exact expiry date, the three stored copies equal to the receipt, replay equal to the receipt and exactly one plaintext between two concurrent creates; H2 to H4 cover renewal receipts, exact-expiry refusal, signed renewal of an expired bearer, the old digest staying refused and the new one serving; H1 fences cover expiry only from terminal issuance and renewal after a lost reply; the legacy migration witness covers rollback, exact credit, null-expiry refusal, renewal with session removal and a malformed expiry; http-idle covers both stream eras closing at the recheck, 401 after, a canceled callback that cannot close a replacement layer, a deadline crossed during listen registration, a deferred opening and an initialization across expiry, and the admitted call.\n\nControls (review package manifest SHA-256 9afeb1bc, 10 payloads and 4 sub-audit manifests verified):\n- Fixed-lifetime control 70000 (/private/tmp/artroom-security-r5c-fixed-lifetime-control-evidence-20261024-v1): 31 days in place of 30 fails 5 and passes 13, at hosted.scope.test.ts:136 twice, 499, the fences case and 1227, each on the independently computed date.\n- Redaction control 42057 (…-redaction-control-evidence-20261024-v1): retainedAnswer as identity fails 5 and passes 13, at the stored-copy check (line 109, three callers), the fences replay at 1099 and the legacy snapshot at 1211. The later registry assertion is not reached under this mutation; the clean baseline covers it.\n- Stream-deadline control 82913 (…-stream-deadline-control-evidence-20261024-v1): the due callback without closeAll fails 1 and passes 3 at http-idle.test.ts:141, observing [2,1,1,0] where [0,0,0,0] was required.\n- All three ran on the head's exact production bytes (hosted.ts SHA-256 e8d5159e and http.ts e5c0c125 at snapshot abb9d60f equal the files at 6015dc3d), with the child exiting 1 naturally, the wrapper 0, and before and after snapshots differing only in the declared Vitest cache cells and the target's change time.\n- Earlier runs 35569, 99714 and 66450 stay recorded as they failed; the continuation 10047 passed the whole Native 18 (sub-audit verified).\n\nGate 11319 at e10584fc (tree a0b8b3c0), raw folder /private/tmp/artroom-security-r5c-gate-evidence-20261024-v1, audited in …-gate-independent-audit-20261024-v1 (manifest SHA-256 b2345e22; 4 payloads verified): result.json records expectedHead e10584fc, expectedTree a0b8b3c0, unchangedCheckpoint true, gatePassed true; before.json and after.json are byte-identical; stdout.log shows all eight stages exit 0 and the npm child exited 0 with no signal. stages/test.log reads \"Test Files 497 passed | 1 skipped (498)\" and \"Tests 3546 passed | 3 skipped (3549)\", zero unhandled; the Node block reports pass 39 fail 0 and the Counting block pass 55 fail 0. The head differs from e10584fc only in the note.\n\nSeals. hosted.ts 12022f8f and http.ts 757f8b36 are the maintained producer's values, and the Node block passed on bytes identical to the head's.\n\nDocument checks at 6015dc3d:\n- git diff --check from Main dbaa3a2a is clean;\n- check-commit-messages from dbaa3a2a reports 11 checked, 0 flagged; the longest subject is 62 characters;\n- section citations on an export report 1,877 resolved, 0 broken and 5 known unresolved; the citation script is identical to Main's;\n- merging the head into Main dbaa3a2a gives exactly its tree, 04c60130.\n\nArchitecture: the deadline lives in the agent row and is enforced at one admission point; the HTTP layer keeps a copy only to tear streams down and is discarded on every rotation; the migration is per object, versioned by a marker in the table the budget already owns, with no new table and no cross-object cutover; the planner's deploy obligations are written where an operator reads them.\nSecurity: I found no defect. Plaintext never reaches SQL, since the one write path for answers redacts and the agent row stores the redacted receipt. Expired and legacy digests fail closed before any MCP body. The migration's SQL is parameterized, paged one row at a time and bounded by the control budget. No route, caller or authority is added; scheduleExpiry is a test port with a production default. Residual, not a defect: a dormant registry keeps a raw creation answer until it activates, and that bearer no longer authenticates anywhere once its agent migrates with a null expiry, so the exposure is to storage readers only and ends with the planner's activation step.\nSimplification: 92 lines in hosted.ts, 88 in http.ts. Nonblocking: http.ts repeats the closed-or-due refusal at five sites; one small helper would read better. Otherwise the shape is proportionate.\n\nResidual notes for the planner's deploy, not defects of this head: renew every live hosted-agent token explicitly and record it (855dd86d); activate the relevant registries through the control plane or record that dormant cleanup stays lazy; a renewal deletes the agent's sessions; hosted MCP stays closed unless MCP_ENABLED is set in the same step (10f45efc).\n\nFindings: F1 required (documentation). Nothing is deployed or claimed deployed by this head. The successor that fixes F1 may be note-only and I will review it against this record.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dcbb45056ac1d86bca31d85f26acf4510bd8c238","binding":"assigned","head":"6015dc3d610da3f4769ecd8a2c00cc3bc59ee98c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9f814f4176de5459ab0e37f5960dc86dd854efd2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fb529297627a453b7f844979779ab0b27867fd15\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0cc4d438e5ff25e46e88547e28e6ada5c92df419","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}